@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Switch}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Accessibility}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Switch @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Accessibility</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Switch @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Accessibility</h1>

<p>
    This Switch component was built following the W3C ARIA Authoring Practices Guide (APG). By adhering to standardised patterns, we ensure that the component
    behaves predictably across different browsers and assistive technologies.
</p>

<h2 id="switch-keyboard">Keyboard interaction</h2>
<ul aria-labelledby="switch-keyboard" class="keyboard-list">
    <li><kbd>Space</kbd> - when focus is on the Switch, toggles the state of the switch.</li>
    <li><kbd>Enter</kbd> - when focus is on the Switch, toggles the state of the switch.</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong>These keyboard interactions are primarily aimed at keyboard-only users. Screen reader users will often navigate differently using their assistive technology's
    built-in commands, though the patterns also apply when a screen reader is operating in interaction mode.
</p>

<h2 id="device-testing">Accessibility device testing</h2>

<ul aria-labelledby="device-testing">
    <li>JAWS, Narrator and NVDA on Windows were each paired with every one of the following browsers: Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge and Mozilla Firefox.</li>
    <li>VoiceOver on macOS was paired with Apple's Safari.</li>
    <li>VoiceOver on iPhone was paired with mobile Safari.</li>
    <li>Talkback on Android was paired with mobile Google Chrome.</li>
    <li>Voice access on Windows 11</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong> Testing was performed with the latest browser and assistive technologies versions that were available at the time of testing (see release history on the installation page for approximate testing dates)
</p>

<h2 id="screen-reader-quirks">Screen reader quirks or known issues</h2>
<ul aria-labelledby="screen-reader-quirks" class="quirks-list">
    <li><b>Narrator</b> paired with <b>Firefox</b> announces button on/off instead of switch on/off.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong> The same quirks were also noted on the APG example.
</p>

<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Switch}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Installation}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Switch - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Switch}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Api}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Switch - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>
